{"id": "3864e3a3-1339-4298-909b-7f90bed1e26b", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T08:58:31.930728", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "6def183d-1d16-49f6-88b7-4e6fac6bd79a", "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "Submitted stage=plan. Workspace survey: /workspace contains only task.json (text states \"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\"); no CycleNet code, configs, docs, notebooks, or dataset loaders are present. Proposed approach: two-stage design — (a) an estimator stage computing ACF, PACF, and FFT-peak candidates on training split within a per-dataset [L_min, L_max] band, (b) a downstream CycleNet evaluation stage varying the injected cycle length with paper-default, lookback, ACF, PACF, FFT, oracle, and random-uniform baselines, across standard CycleNet benchmark datasets (ETTh1/h2/m1/m2, Weather, Electricity, Traffic, Exchange), horizons in {96, 192, 336, 720}, fixed splits, ≥3 seeds, MSE/MAE primary and oracle-gap secondary metrics, plus a sensitivity matrix over estimator choice, top-k, band, detrending, and horizon/lookback. Consequential assumptions, design choices, and uncertainties enumerated separately and explicitly listed for researcher sign-off before the full design is drafted. Awaiting reviewer approval; no full design produced yet.", "evidence": "Inspection commands run: `ls -la /workspace` (output shows only `task.json`); `find /workspace -type f` (output: `/workspace/task.json` only); `cat /workspace/task.json` (output fields: question, context, documents.track.md whose literal text reads 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.'). No README, .py, .yaml/.json config, .ipynb, dataset loaders, or scripts related to CycleNet, autocorrelation, period selection, or forecasting benchmarks were found in /workspace. The two-stage proposed approach is described in the answer body; the experiment-design choices, assumptions, and uncertainties to resolve are enumerated in answer section (3).", "assumptions": ["CycleNet exposes its cycle length as a fixed integer hyperparameter consumed by Residual Periodic Encoding; no architectural change is required to vary the length.", "Standard CycleNet benchmark datasets, train/val/test split conventions, lookback/horizon protocols, and metrics are those used in the CycleNet paper (Informer-family protocol).", "Estimator stage operates on training data only to prevent leakage into val/test.", "A per-dataset candidate band [L_min, L_max] exists (e.g., 24/96/168/365 for daily/half-hourly/weekly/yearly-scale series) such that the paper-default length lies inside it.", "Each series has a single dominant periodicity; multi-period ensembling is out of scope unless the researcher asks otherwise.", "Compute posture is design-only in /workspace; implementation will rely on stdlib + NumPy/PyTorch as needed once the design is approved."], "uncertainties": ["Whether CycleNet in the intended setup accepts arbitrary integer cycle lengths or only canonical ones (24, 96, 168, 365).", "Preferred dataset list beyond the standard eight, and the exact horizon/lookback protocol to use.", "Whether 'optimal' length is defined as best mean MSE across horizons, best MSE on the longest (or shortest) horizon, or a robust rank aggregate.", "Whether to restrict datasets to those where CycleNet publishes a default length or to include novel datasets.", "Whether autocorrelation analysis applies per-channel or to a globally aggregated series, which scales experiment cost by number of channels.", "Whether PACF should be retained (more interpretable for cycle boundaries) or only ACF+FFT are required.", "Number of seeds (3 vs. 5) and the statistical-comparison convention (paired t vs. rank-based) for the headline claim."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-ad736462-dd31-4d64-a013-fd29743b8031", "tool_call": {"id": "call-ad736462-dd31-4d64-a013-fd29743b8031", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Propose CycleNet cycle-length experiment plan\", \"stage\": \"plan\", \"answer\": \"Submitted stage=plan. Workspace survey: /workspace contains only task.json (text states \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\"); no CycleNet code, configs, docs, notebooks, or dataset loaders are present. Proposed approach: two-stage design \\u2014 (a) an estimator stage computing ACF, PACF, and FFT-peak candidates on training split within a per-dataset [L_min, L_max] band, (b) a downstream CycleNet evaluation stage varying the injected cycle length with paper-default, lookback, ACF, PACF, FFT, oracle, and random-uniform baselines, across standard CycleNet benchmark datasets (ETTh1/h2/m1/m2, Weather, Electricity, Traffic, Exchange), horizons in {96, 192, 336, 720}, fixed splits, \\u22653 seeds, MSE/MAE primary and oracle-gap secondary metrics, plus a sensitivity matrix over estimator choice, top-k, band, detrending, and horizon/lookback. Consequential assumptions, design choices, and uncertainties enumerated separately and explicitly listed for researcher sign-off before the full design is drafted. Awaiting reviewer approval; no full design produced yet.\", \"evidence\": \"Inspection commands run: `ls -la /workspace` (output shows only `task.json`); `find /workspace -type f` (output: `/workspace/task.json` only); `cat /workspace/task.json` (output fields: question, context, documents.track.md whose literal text reads 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.'). No README, .py, .yaml/.json config, .ipynb, dataset loaders, or scripts related to CycleNet, autocorrelation, period selection, or forecasting benchmarks were found in /workspace. The two-stage proposed approach is described in the answer body; the experiment-design choices, assumptions, and uncertainties to resolve are enumerated in answer section (3).\", \"assumptions\": [\"CycleNet exposes its cycle length as a fixed integer hyperparameter consumed by Residual Periodic Encoding; no architectural change is required to vary the length.\", \"Standard CycleNet benchmark datasets, train/val/test split conventions, lookback/horizon protocols, and metrics are those used in the CycleNet paper (Informer-family protocol).\", \"Estimator stage operates on training data only to prevent leakage into val/test.\", \"A per-dataset candidate band [L_min, L_max] exists (e.g., 24/96/168/365 for daily/half-hourly/weekly/yearly-scale series) such that the paper-default length lies inside it.\", \"Each series has a single dominant periodicity; multi-period ensembling is out of scope unless the researcher asks otherwise.\", \"Compute posture is design-only in /workspace; implementation will rely on stdlib + NumPy/PyTorch as needed once the design is approved.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Whether CycleNet in the intended setup accepts arbitrary integer cycle lengths or only canonical ones (24, 96, 168, 365).\", \"Preferred dataset list beyond the standard eight, and the exact horizon/lookback protocol to use.\", \"Whether 'optimal' length is defined as best mean MSE across horizons, best MSE on the longest (or shortest) horizon, or a robust rank aggregate.\", \"Whether to restrict datasets to those where CycleNet publishes a default length or to include novel datasets.\", \"Whether autocorrelation analysis applies per-channel or to a globally aggregated series, which scales experiment cost by number of channels.\", \"Whether PACF should be retained (more interpretable for cycle boundaries) or only ACF+FFT are required.\", \"Number of seeds (3 vs. 5) and the statistical-comparison convention (paired t vs. rank-based) for the headline claim.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-f2a76087-6b9b-4e74-898e-48f60d99f8bc", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 12}
